import json,pathlib
p=pathlib.Path(__file__).parent;d=json.loads((p/'score-audit.json').read_text())
lines=['# Audit of the other four NexusPoint editions','','**Completed source and scoring audit; corrected drafts only. Nothing scheduled or deployed.**','','The earlier review missed additional timing problems. Dodgers used late MLB article updates for public game results. New York used later reporting where original announcement posts were available and incorrectly assigned event dates to retrospective court/archive records. These have been corrected. Trump broadcast bounds were tightened and unsupported source wording removed. The Fed release times and scores were already correct.','','All 20 cards pass the study and pre-reveal evidence checks; all 100 measurement windows are usable. Original CSV prices, scoring windows, initial card orders and the one-point tie threshold are unchanged. Full raw-price reconstruction and bounded fresh provider comparisons are documented in [data audit](data-audit.md). These are sampled provider rechecks, not a new download of every historical observation.','','## Editorial disposition','','| Edition | Outcome | Remaining limit |','|---|---|---|','| Fed | Release times verified; five ranks stable | Provider creation/start metadata differ; exact-token early observations are retained and freshly corroborated. |','| Trump | Tighter broadcast bounds; five scores unchanged | Debate/Iowa tie splits in a −1h diagnostic. Butler’s measured window begins after the shots, at confirmed reporting; the earlier jump can enter the reference. |','| NYC | Earlier announcement evidence; primary jump unchanged | Endorsement tie changes at +1h. Original NYT publication minutes remain unverified, so do not present the small-card ranking as robust. |','| Dodgers | Official live-event times recover NLDS +11 pp | Three low-response cards tie. Groups stable at ±1h, but a wider earlier Glasnow disclosure scenario can split the low group. |','','The corrected scores are usable descriptive measurements. The table above is **not blanket approval of four equally strong ranking games**. Fed is the clearest. Trump/NYC close comparisons and the Dodgers three-card tie require editorial acceptance before scheduling. A larger measured move is not proof of isolated causal impact.','','## Corrected scores and timing','','Changes are percentage points in the median YES-contract price: 12h before the supported public cutoff versus 18–36h afterward. The original scoring profile is preserved.']
for e in d['editions']:
 lines += ['', '### '+e['topic'],'','| Card | Previous | Corrected | Corrected public cutoff (UTC) |','|---|---:|---:|---|']
 for c in e['cards']:
  fmt=lambda x:f'{0 if abs(x)<1e-10 else x:+.3f}'.rstrip('0').rstrip('.')
  lines.append(f"| {c['title']} | {fmt(c['oldPp'])} | {fmt(c['newPp'])} | {c['cutoff']} |")
 names={c['id']:c['title'] for c in e['cards']};lines+=['','**Ranking groups:** '+' → '.join(' = '.join(names[i] for i in g) for g in e['tieGroups'])+'.','',f"[Exact revised draft]({pathlib.Path(e['study']).resolve()})"]
lines += ['', '## Important source corrections','','- Trump: conviction wording now states the jury verdict rather than claiming a timestamped DA announcement. Iowa’s unsupported 808-person detail was removed. The first CNN marker precedes the poll text; the correct full-claim upper bound is 23:05:01 UTC. The debate card uses a historical live-broadcast record, distinct from publication of its later replay.','- NYC: the retained AOC Bluesky post was by Mamdani, not AOC. The earlier NY1 confirmation now anchors that card. Original Cuomo, Hochul and Adams posts replace later coverage. The concession uses an eyewitness post from 02:26 UTC, supported by the live blog. Court, archive and election-result pages no longer carry fabricated historical publication times.','- Dodgers: the one-inning Ohtani debut is complete when Banda replaces him at 02:31:59.850 UTC. This is distinct from the June15 announcement, the bottom of the first inning, and the end of the full game. The NLDS result is 01:39:19.872 UTC; the old 07:11 article update was over five hours late.','- Provenance: Trump and NYC had the CSV hash labeled as raw and a separate JSON hash labeled as normalized. The repaired drafts now point to raw-response bundles with per-file checksums and use the exact CSV hash as normalized. No historical observations changed.', '- Fed: Powell’s official release-on-delivery PDF establishes 10:00 a.m. EDT. BLS releases state their 8:30 a.m. ET embargo. Minor jobs-report wording and basis-point units were clarified.','','## Sensitivity limits','','The Fed and corrected Dodgers tie groups remain the same at ±1h. Reordering two IDs inside a tied group does not count as a changed ranking. Trump’s debate/Iowa pair splits at −1h. NYC’s two endorsement cards split at +1h.','','Broader scenarios are diagnostics, not alternative timestamps chosen to improve scores. Moving the unresolved AOC publication bound six hours earlier produces +2.55 pp instead of +0.20; that is a reason to disclose uncertainty, not claim the endorsement caused that larger move. Moving Glasnow’s bound three hours earlier produces +0.5 rather than 0 and splits the small-response group.','','For Dodgers, a separate six-hour pre-first-play baseline gives NLDS +11, pennant +2.5, Ohtani 0 and seventh loss −1 pp. This supports the larger playoff movement without relying on a reference that includes in-game trading.','','## Reproducible evidence','','- [Complete scores, windows and sensitivity](score-audit.json)','- [Independent Trump evidence audit](trump/audit.md) and [corrected transcript brackets](trump/tighter-anchors.md)','- [Fed primary-source audit](fed/audit.md)','- [NYC exact evidence and correction ledger](nyc/anchor-freeze.json)','- [Dodgers parent-verified correction ledger](dodgers/anchor-freeze.json); this supersedes preliminary worker timing notes where they differ.','- [Data provenance and fresh provider checks](data-audit.md)','- [Full five-day approval review](../APPROVAL-REVIEW.md)','','Runtime schedule, registry and approval hashes are unchanged. All underlying outcomes have concluded; endings remain reveal-only.']
(p/'REVIEW.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
